{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1299790-2e-dullahan-writeup","id":1299790,"title":"[2E] Dullahan Writeup","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-25T17:34:38-07:00","id":1299790,"title":"[2E] Dullahan Writeup","content":"So I'm thinking of running a Scion game in the near future\u2013I ran a couple in 1e, and I'm intrigued enough by 2e to take a crack at it\u2013and with the ability opened up to play adopted Scions and fantastical creatures adopted under other gods, my wife knew what she wanted to do.<br /> <br /> Having seen too much Durarara!!, she wants to play a Dullahan (one of the characters is one). Without a writeup that I could find, I figured I could write one up; I do homebrew for my Exalted games, and this is little different in practice. <br /> <br /> What follows is first an Antagonist writeup, then the Calling. I've erred slightly on the side of letting one blend in (the usual description of a Dullahan's visage being compared to a cross-section of yeasty bread, or moldy cheese), and I might have overtuned the Antagonist writeup. But I want to know what other people have to say.<br /> <br /> So without further ado:<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Antagonist Block</span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Archetype</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Nemesis</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Qualities</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Perfected Soldier, Unstoppable, Apocalyptic Presence, Unnatural Behavior (Must flee the presence of gold)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Flairs</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Curse, Here I Come</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drive</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Name, Hunt, and Take Prey</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Pool</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 11 (Attack (+3e), Intimidate, Track)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Secondary Pool</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 9 (Ride, Athletics, Magic)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Desperation Pool</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 6</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Health</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 7</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Defense</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 5</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Initiative</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 9</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Extras</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Mystic Arsenal (Spine Whip, see below for relic stats. Tags: Melee, Lethal, Messy, Reach, Versatile. Grants access to the Death Purview, although the Dullahan can only use Marvels)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Description</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Reapers of souls and markers of the doomed, the Dullahans (Also known as </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Gan Ceann, </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">the Headless Man) ride across the ages; although they now sit astride motorcycles and in sports cars instead of black steeds or the bone wagon known as the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>coiste bodha</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (or coach-a-bower) of centuries past, their passage still strikes eyes blind, and while they open their slasher-smile mouths only to speak the names of their victims, their voice still can still strike mortals dead; some few have thought themselves lucky enough to survive, only for fate to catch up with them hours or days later.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Originally the Dullahans served Crom Cruach in his guise as Crom Dubh, as his agents of fear, retribution, and dominance; even after Crom Cruach had his war with Patricius and was driven away, deep and slumbering, his emissary rode out to remind the people that he would come again.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In the modern day Dullahans remain rare; the powerful and unscrupulous have used them as assassins; being powerful and unscrupulous themselves, the Gan Ceann have no moral objections, but few are inclined to do their natural work at the behest of a mortal. Some have managed it, usually either through making a bargain with the creature itself or with a greater power that can command them. Some few have attempted to gain leverage over the Gan Ceann directly, either through stealing their head or some attempt at sorcerous binding; to date this has yet to work as anything but a spectacularly creative suicide.<br /> <br /> ****</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dullahan Calling</span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Example Calling Keywords</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Horror, Omen, Rider, Inescapable, Dread</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Path Skills</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Pilot, Persuasion</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Path Contacts</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Criminals, morticians, ghosts</span></span><br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><img src=\"https://docs.google.com/drawings/d/sbRoT0hJTvPYqYPMfP1a_Xw/image?w=605&amp;h=346&amp;rev=11&amp;ac=1&amp;parent=1vQs6AK0XCL6m-rPK01jJ22SvsfYOXcB4ubFqQWEovPc\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While Scions have put some Dullahans to rest throughout history, new souls join their number to replace them. Crom Dubh, even in his sleep, usually snaps these up into his keeping, where they are bent to his will. Some other Tuatha, those who have an affinity for Death, have marked souls as their own instead, and have stayed the crooked god\u2019s hand. Such Dullahans are still monstrous, terrifying, and agents of death, but at least their will is their own; if their fate cannot be denied, it can at least be bargained with.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Heroic Knacks</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Inevitable Entry</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: You may open any door within arm\u2019s reach without touching it; you may also attempt to pick or break locks in your way without any penalties or complications for lack of tools.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cloak of Dread:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> [As the Leader Knack]</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dark Harbinger</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Speaking the character\u2019s name, you make an opposed Knack Skill roll. Success resolves its remaining successes as stunts of a Thrown Attack and inflicts the wound condition Fated Death: the target suffers its penalty under potentially lethal circumstances, accidental or otherwise. This power can only be used once a scene.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Night Rider</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Take any Heroic Hunter Knack.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Soul Taker</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: If a character dies in the same field as you, you may spend 1 Momentum to catch its soul in your head, preventing it from moving on to whatever would await it after death. Other ghosts may also be captured, but require a contested Knack Skill roll.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Immortal Knacks</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Enter Nightmare</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Any time you invoke a Dullahan Knack or spend momentum or legend to invoke this Path, make a Shift Atmosphere roll at +1 scale. Success nudges the area towards an aura of creeping fear and dread.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">No Witnesses</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Spend two momentum and make a Knack Skill roll to intimidate those in the area. Onlookers of the Dullahan\u2019s tier suffer excruciating pain and are compelled to look away; they can continue to attempt to interact or even confront the Dullahan, but suffer a +2 Complication. Failing to buy this off inflicts a wound condition to the viewer inflicting blindness in one eye; vision returns with healing for Scions and other creatures, but this is permanent for mortals.</span></span><br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dullahan\u2019s Whip</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Relic</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> ****)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Enhancement</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: +1 to all uses</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Purview</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Death</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Motif</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>You can\u2019t run forever</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The spine whips of the Dullahans are terrifying weapons, though the eerie presence of the Gan Ceann means few provide enough resistance to merit their use. Each one is neatly polished, yellowed with age, and held together with sinew. Each one is far, far too long to have come from a single human body (and the few who have been able to examine them have confirmed they cannot be anything but). All of Crom Cruach\u2019s own Dullahans wield one, forged from bloody sacrifices in his name; other Tuatha tend to consider it a distasteful weapon, but the few who have adopted a soul out of Crom Cruach\u2019s clutches have been known (very rarely) to overcome their own misgivings\u2026although where they acquire one is unknown.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tags</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Melee, Lethal, Messy, Reach, Versatile</span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}